{"availability":"available","full":"wileewang/TransPixeler","name":"TransPixeler","description":"CVPR2025","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":927,"forks":70,"created":"2024-12-24T06:37:35Z","updated":"2025-05-14T05:25:17Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/wileewang/TransPixar","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T01:08:41.999Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T01:08:41.999Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T01:08:41.999Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T01:08:41.999Z","stars":927,"forks":70}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Luozhou Wang, Yijun Li, Zhifei Chen, Jui-Hsien Wang, Zhifei Zhang, He Zhang, Zhe Lin, Ying-Cong Chen†","\\ Internship Project \\ Project Lead † Corresponding Author","Text-to-video generative models have made significant strides, enabling diverse applications in entertainment, advertising, and education. However, generating RGBA video, which includes alpha channels for transparency, remains a challenge due to limited datasets and the difficulty of adapting existing models. Alpha channels are crucial for visual effects (VFX), allowing transparent elements like smoke and reflections to blend seamlessly into scenes. We introduce TransPixar, a method to extend pretrained video models for RGBA generation while retaining the original RGB capabilities. TransPixar…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/wileewang/TransPixeler/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8735029c36d57413148e80a9b8bef68bdfca31b2b5ef10141c4c143ac31f464c","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T01:08:42.110Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T01:08:42.110Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Luozhou Wang, Yijun Li, Zhifei Chen, Jui-Hsien Wang, Zhifei Zhang, He Zhang, Zhe Lin, Ying-Cong Chen†","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/wileewang/TransPixeler/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"8735029c36d57413148e80a